[2026-01-30T12:19:01.116Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Implementation: Decompose 633-line Scenes.tsx into focused scene components with shared animation primitives\n\n## Context Area\nData Visualizations\n\n## Description\nDecompose 633-line Scenes.tsx into focused scene components with shared animation primitives\n\n## Implementation Details\n\n## Vision\nDecompose the monolithic Scenes.tsx (633 lines) into smaller, focused scene components with shared animation primitives. Currently, ChartsScene (124 lines), InsightsScene (129 lines), and SummaryScene (100 lines) contain significant duplication in layout patterns, header rendering, and animation setup.\n\n## Business Value\n- Improves maintainability by breaking 600+ line file into focused modules\n- Enables parallel development on different scenes\n- Makes scene composition more flexible for future video formats\n- Reduces cognitive load when modifying individual scenes\n\n## Scope\n**Included:**\n- Extract shared scene layout primitives (SceneHeader, SceneContainer)\n- Split each scene into its own file with shared imports\n- Create scene animation presets for common patterns\n\n**Excluded:**\n- Video playback core (already well-structured)\n- Template configuration system (separate concern)\n\n## Key Components\n1. `SceneHeader` - reusable header with title, icon bar, and line animation\n2. `SceneContainer` - consistent padding and background handling\n3. `useSceneAnimations` - preset animation timing for common patterns\n4. Individual scene files: TitleScene.tsx, MetricsScene.tsx, etc.\n\n## Technical Approach\n1. Identify repeated patterns in current Scenes.tsx\n2. Create shared primitives for header and container patterns\n3. Extract each scene function to its own file\n4. Create animation presets for common spring configurations\n5. Update barrel exports in scenes/index.tsx\n6. Verify visual parity with before/after comparison\n\n## Files to Modify\n- Split: `src/components/report/video/Scenes.tsx` into:\n  - `src/components/report/video/scenes/TitleScene.tsx`\n  - `src/components/report/video/scenes/MetricsScene.tsx`\n  - `src/components/report/video/scenes/ChartsScene.tsx`\n  - `src/components/report/video/scenes/InsightsScene.tsx`\n  - `src/components/report/video/scenes/SummaryScene.tsx`\n  - `src/components/report/video/scenes/primitives.tsx`\n- Update: `src/components/report/video/index.tsx` exports\n\n## Success Criteria\n- [ ] Each scene is in its own file under 100 lines\n- [ ] Shared primitives are extracted and reused\n- [ ] Visual output is identical before and after refactor\n- [ ] No breaking changes to existing VideoOverview integration\n\n## Potential Challenges\n- Ensuring animation timing stays consistent - mitigate with visual regression testing\n- Circular dependencies between primitives and scenes - mitigate with careful module structure\n\n\n## Instructions\n\n1. Read and understand the implementation details above\n2. Identify all files that need to be modified\n3. Implement the changes following the guidance provided\n4. Ensure code quality and type safety\n5. Test the changes work as expected\n\n## Notes\n\nThis requirement was generated from an accepted Development Direction.\nFocus on implementing exactly what is described above.\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9cec20cb-b613-4ab4-b437-0d4075a2df3d","uuid":"739e730b-d18d-450b-9777-fb07d42ae385","isSynthetic":true}
